  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the files needed to trace the full chain:\n\n1. **`pkg/registry/core/rest/storage_core.go`** \u2014 where the PostStartHook `\"start-service-ip-repair-controllers\"` is registered and where `\"unable to perform initial IP and Port allocation check\"` is generated after a 1-minute timeout waiting for the repair controllers' `onFirstSuccess` callbacks.\n2. **`pkg/registry/core/service/ipallocator/controller/repairip.go`** \u2014 the `RepairIPAddress` controller (`RunUntil`/`doRunOnce`/`syncService`) that creates `IPAddress` objects during its initial reconcile pass; this is the caller that gets the \"forbidden: not yet ready\" response.\n3. **`staging/.../admission/plugin/namespace/lifecycle/admission.go`** \u2014 source of the literal `\"not yet ready to handle request\"` forbidden error, gated on `WaitForReady()`/informer `HasSynced`, which is the race during rolling upgrade (repair controller races admission-plugin informer sync).\n4. **`staging/.../server/healthz/healthz.go`** and **`hooks.go`** \u2014 how PostStartHook failures get wired into `/readyz` as `poststarthook/...` checks, and the `informer-sync` checker referenced in the ticket's readyz output.\n5. **`config.go`** \u2014 `AddPostStartHookOrDie` registration mechanics.\n6. Supporting admission plugins with the same \"not yet ready\" pattern (`policy/generic/plugin.go`, `webhook/generic/webhook.go`) since any of these can produce the forbidden error depending on which plugin's cache hasn't synced.\n7. **`defaultservicecidr.go`** and **`ipallocator.go`** \u2014 the default ServiceCIDR wait and IP allocator context that the repair controller depends on before it can succeed, relevant to the mixed-version race.\n8. **`test/e2e/apimachinery/health_handlers.go`** \u2014 shows expected healthy readyz output for cross-reference against the failure in the ticket.",
